;; FH-REACT-003 — the exported component is one object, and stays one across a
;; reload.
;;
;; React reconciles on component TYPE. Everything in this row follows from that
;; single fact: a bridge that answered a fresh function per call would instruct
;; React to unmount and rebuild the foreign library's whole subtree every time
;; the exporting expression ran — losing a grid's scroll offset, a chart's
;; animation state and an editor's selection for no reason at all. That is
;; exactly the bug a hand-written wrapper ships, and removing it is most of why
;; this verb exists.
;;
;; The reload arm is the one that decides the CACHE KEY, and it is the assertion
;; that distinguishes a correct implementation from a plausible one. A hot
;; reload mints a FRESH descriptor object for the same view, so a cache keyed on
;; descriptor identity is a cache that misses on every reload — technically
;; memoised, and a remount in practice. Keying on the view id makes the reload a
;; republication: same component, new body.
;;
;; `:distinct` is the guard against over-sharing. Identity must not be so eager
;; that two genuinely different exports collapse into one, so both axes of the
;; key are proven to separate.
{:fh/id "FH-REACT-003"
 :fh/law
 "Exporting one view with one adapter answers the IDENTICAL component object every time, including across a redefinition of the view — which republishes the new body through the component React already mounted rather than minting a new type — while a different adapter over the same view, and the same adapter over a different view, are each a different component."

 ;; Repeated exports of one view.
 :repeats 3

 ;; The reload. The same view id, a genuinely different descriptor object, and
 ;; a body whose output moved — so the republication is observable rather than
 ;; merely asserted.
 :reload
 {:view-id       :re-frame.freehand.to-react-views/reloadable
  :before        "person 7"
  :after         "PERSON 7"
  :same-component true
  :note "a fresh descriptor for the same id must not mint a fresh component type"}

 ;; Both axes of the cache key separate.
 :distinct
 [{:note "the same view under two different adapters"
   :axis :adapter}
  {:note "two different views under no adapter"
   :axis :view}]

 ;; The two views the `:view` axis uses.
 :views
 {:a :re-frame.freehand.to-react-views/person-cell
  :b :re-frame.freehand.to-react-views/badge}}
